@page "/density"

<PageTitle>Hexbins &amp; hex tile maps - Blazor-ApexMaps</PageTitle>

<h1>Hexbins &amp; hex tile maps</h1>

<p class="lead">
    Two answers to the same problem: a map whose real shape gets in the way of its data. One bins
    the points, the other replaces the regions.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Hexbin: more points than pixels</h2>

<div class="demo-toolbar">
    <label>
        Aggregate
        <select class="form-select form-select-sm" value="@_aggregate"
                @onchange="e => Set(() => _aggregate = Enum.Parse<HexbinAggregate>(e.Value?.ToString() ?? nameof(HexbinAggregate.Count)))">
            @foreach (var aggregate in Enum.GetValues<HexbinAggregate>())
            {
                <option value="@aggregate">@aggregate</option>
            }
        </select>
    </label>
    <label>
        Radius
        <select class="form-select form-select-sm" value="@_radius" @onchange="SetRadius">
            <option value="8">8 px</option>
            <option value="14">14 px (default)</option>
            <option value="22">22 px</option>
        </select>
    </label>
    <label>
        Orientation
        <select class="form-select form-select-sm" value="@_orientation"
                @onchange="e => Set(() => _orientation = Enum.Parse<HexbinOrientation>(e.Value?.ToString() ?? nameof(HexbinOrientation.Pointy)))">
            <option value="@HexbinOrientation.Pointy">Pointy (default)</option>
            <option value="@HexbinOrientation.Flat">Flat</option>
        </select>
    </label>
    <div class="form-check form-switch">
        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="gap" checked="@_gap"
               @onchange="e => Set(() => _gap = (bool?)e.Value ?? false)" />
        <label class="form-check-label" for="gap">Gap between cells</label>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="demo-card">
    <ApexMaps Options="_hexbinOptions" Height="520" />
</div>

<p class="text-muted small">
    @SampleData.StormReports.Length.ToString("N0") generated readings around twenty US metros. A
    bubble series at this count is a smear; the lattice is a count you can read. The radius is in
    <em>screen</em> pixels, not world units, so the cells stay the size you chose as you zoom and
    the lattice refines instead of magnifying. That also means the class breaks move when you cross
    a zoom level: the same colour stands for fewer points per cell once the cells are smaller. Pin
    a domain if two maps have to be compared. <code>Count</code> is the default and needs no value
    field, which is the honest answer to "where are these things".
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-5">Hex tile map: every region the same size</h2>

<div class="demo-toolbar">
    <div class="form-check form-switch">
        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="layout" checked="@_hexLayout"
               @onchange="e => Set(() => _hexLayout = (bool?)e.Value ?? false)" />
        <label class="form-check-label" for="layout">Hex layout</label>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="demo-card">
    <ApexMaps Options="_layoutOptions" Height="520" />
</div>

<p class="text-muted small">
    The same choropleth, the same rows, one option. Toggle it and each state walks to its cell
    rather than the map being swapped, which is how a reader learns which cell is which. A
    cartogram is a deliberate choice, not a default: it is right when the story is about people or
    money and land area actively misleads, and when small states have to stay legible. It is wrong
    when a reader needs to navigate by geography. The layout downloads independently of the
    boundaries and is roughly fifty times smaller, so this form does not fetch geometry it never
    draws.
</p>

<p class="text-muted small">
    Both are licensed features. Without a key they work in full, with a watermark, so you can
    evaluate them on your own data.
</p>

@code {
    private HexbinAggregate _aggregate = HexbinAggregate.Count;
    private double _radius = 14;
    private HexbinOrientation _orientation = HexbinOrientation.Pointy;
    private bool _gap = true;
    private bool _hexLayout = true;

    private MapsOptions _hexbinOptions = null!;
    private MapsOptions _layoutOptions = null!;

    protected override void OnInitialized() => Rebuild();

    private void Set(Action change)
    {
        change();
        Rebuild();
    }

    // A method rather than an inline lambda: the parse needs a string literal for the fallback,
    // and a nested double quote ends the Razor attribute.
    private void SetRadius(ChangeEventArgs e) =>
        Set(() => _radius = double.TryParse(e.Value?.ToString(), out var radius) ? radius : 14);

    private void Rebuild()
    {
        _hexbinOptions = new MapsOptions
        {
            Geo = new GeoOptions
            {
                Map = GeoMaps.UsStates,
                View = new ViewOptions { Fit = new GeoBounds(-125, 24, -66, 50), Padding = 16 },
            },
            Series =
            [
                new HexbinSeries
                {
                    Name = "Readings",
                    Data = SampleData.StormReports,
                    Aggregate = _aggregate,
                    Radius = _radius,
                    Orientation = _orientation,
                    Gap = _gap ? 0.12 : 0,
                    MinCount = 1,
                    Scale = new ScaleOptions { Palette = Palettes.Viridis, Classes = 6 },
                },
            ],
            Legend = new LegendOptions
            {
                Position = LegendPosition.Bottom,
                Title = _aggregate == HexbinAggregate.Count ? "Readings per cell" : $"{_aggregate} of reading",
            },
            Tooltip = new TooltipOptions
            {
                Formatter = JsFunction.From("ctx => `<b>${ctx.value ?? 0}</b> in this cell`"),
            },
        };

        _layoutOptions = new MapsOptions
        {
            Geo = new GeoOptions
            {
                Map = GeoMaps.UsStates,
                Layout = _hexLayout ? MapLayout.Hex : null,
            },
            Series =
            [
                new ChoroplethSeries
                {
                    Name = "Broadband adoption (%)",
                    // us/states joins on `abbr`, which is the key that pack recommends.
                    JoinBy = "abbr",
                    Data = SampleData.Broadband,
                    Scale = new ScaleOptions { Palette = Palettes.Blues, Classes = 5 },
                },
            ],
            // Chart-level data labels rather than the series' own: a hex tile map that does not
            // name its cells is unreadable, because the whole point is that the shapes no longer
            // tell you where you are. Every cell is the same size, so there is no small-feature
            // case to skip and no collisions to resolve.
            DataLabels = new DataLabelOptions
            {
                Enabled = true,
                Field = "abbr",
                Collision = LabelCollision.Hide,
                MinFeatureArea = 0,
                Style = new DataLabelStyle { FontSize = 11, FontWeight = 600 },
            },
            Legend = new LegendOptions { Position = LegendPosition.Bottom },
            Tooltip = new TooltipOptions
            {
                Formatter = JsFunction.From("ctx => `<b>${ctx.name}</b><br>${ctx.value ?? '-'}%`"),
            },
        };
    }
}
